{"name":"Ninja Princess","hex":"#75528b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ninja","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One trained in ninjutsu, especially one used for espionage, assassination, and other tasks requiring stealth during Japan's shogunate period.","One who very skillful, considered similar to the historical ninja, especially in covert or stealthy operation."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fast and sneaky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ninja"},{"term":"princess","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A female member of a royal family other than a queen, especially a daughter or granddaughter of a monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A woman or girl who excels in a given field or class."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/princess"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sega Ninja","blocks":[{"text":"Sega Ninja, originally released as Ninja Princess in Japan, is a 1985 run and gun video game developed and published by Sega for arcades. The player controls Princess Kurumi, the titular female ninja, who battles enemies using throwing knives and shurikens. In contrast to most later games in the genre, Ninja Princess has a feudal Japan setting with a female ninja protagonist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4d/Sega_Ninja_arcade_flyer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sega_Ninja","wikidata":"Q3477719"},{"title":"Ninja","blocks":[{"text":"A ninja , shinobi no mono  or shinobi  was a spy and infiltrator in pre-modern Japan. Antecedents may have existed as early as the 12th century. Despite popular belief, there is little evidence that ninja were assassins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/72/Hokusai-sketches---hokusai-manga-vol6-crop.jpg/330px-Hokusai-sketches---hokusai-manga-vol6-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ninja","wikidata":"Q9402"},{"title":"Princess","blocks":[{"text":"Princess is a title used by a female member of a regnant monarch's family or by a female ruler of a principality. The male equivalent is a prince. Most often, the term has been used for the consort of a prince, or for the daughter of a monarch. A crown princess can be the heir apparent to the throne or the spouse of the heir apparent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg/330px-Sigrid_Eriksdotter_Vasa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Princess","wikidata":"Q863048"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6c/Seganinja.png/250px-Seganinja.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6c/Seganinja.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6c/Seganinja.png/250px-Seganinja.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeganinja.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/The_ninja.jpg/330px-The_ninja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/89/The_ninja.jpg/330px-The_ninja.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sega Ninja was released as The Ninja for the Master System (pictured: box, cartridge and instructions)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_ninja.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Yamato_Takeru_at_16-crop.jpg/500px-Yamato_Takeru_at_16-crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=t